to the flow computer for printing deliveries, events and alarms.\"\n\nrecommendation:\n- id: \"R117-1\" — hmm canonical \"R117\"? The recommendation is \"R 117-1 (2007)\". Rule: id canonical e.g. \"R60\". For R 117-1, canonical could be \"R117-1\". I'll use \"R117-1\", edition 2007. Wait, edition for R 117-1 is the year 2007 edition. The certificate number says R 117/2007 — the /2007 is the cert scheme year? Actually \"R 117/2007-A-NL1-22.02\" — R117/2007 refers to the Recommendation edition. I'll set edition: 2007. Amendment: null. scheme: \"A\". accuracy_classes: [0.3, 0.5, 1.0].\n\ntest_reports: main TER + component reports + documentation folders. Roles:\n- NMi-2638810-01: type_evaluation_report, date 2022-04-07, pages 50.\n- Component reports: role \"test_report\".\n- Documentation folders (T12216-1, TC12118-1, TC7056-13, TC7057-17, TC8519-4, TC7311-7, TC11730-1, TC7329-5): role \"documentation_file\", no date/pages.\n\nThat's ~8 + 57 + 1 = 66 entries. Long but fine. Actually let me count component reports:\n\nMechanical measurement transducer: 2\nSensor: 12\nCore processor: 17\nFlow transmitter: 10 (incl. duplicate NMi-2571596-01 twice with different page counts — include both as listed; note: maybe second is -02 misOCR'd; record as given? Recording exact duplicate number with different pages is faithful to source. I'll include both but the duplicate id may look odd. I'll include as listed.)\nHmm — \"No. NMi-2571596-01 dated 30 September 2021 that include 38 pages; No. NMi-2571596-01 dated 30 September 2021 that include 32 pages\" — likely OCR error for -02. I'll record both entries as given. Or combine? Don't fabricate — record as-is.\nMultiLoad II: 6\nMASTERLOAD: 2\nGas extractor: 1\nTotal = 50 component reports + 1 TER.\n\nDo I need to include all? Yes, thoroughness. It's long but OK.\n\nAlso documentation folder for the construction of the measuring instrument: T12216-1.\n\nNow matrix_tables details.\n\nTable 3 matrix (BMxx):\nname: \"Specific characteristics of the meter type BMxx (measurement transducer)\"\ncolumns: [\"type\", \"accuracy_class\", \"flange_size\", \"cyclic_volume\", \"qmin\", \"qmax\", \"mmq\"]\ncolumn_units: [null, null, \"inch\", \"L\", \"L/min\", \"L/min\", \"L\"]\nrows:\n{\"type\": \"BM250 (S)\", \"accuracy_class\": 0.3, \"flange_size\": \"2½\\\" (DN 65)\", \"cyclic_volume\": 2.27, \"qmin\": 115, \"qmax\": 1140, \"mmq\": 100}\n{\"type\": \"BM950 (S)\", 0.3, \"3\\\" (DN 80)\", 2.27, 115, 1500, 200}\n{\"type\": \"BM450 (D)\", 0.3, \"3\\\" (DN 80)\", 4.54, 200, 2050, 200}\n{\"type\": \"BM550 (D)\", 0.3, \"4\\\" (DN 100)\", 4.54, 220, 2280, 500}\n{\"type\": \"BM350 (D)\", 0.3, \"4\\\" (DN 100)\", 4.54, 125, 2800, 500}\n{\"type\": \"BM650 (T)\", 0.3, \"4\\\" (DN 100)\", 6.81, 300, 3000, 500}\n{\"type\": \"BM850 (T)\", 0.3, \"6\\\" (DN 150)\", 6.81, 200, 4250, 500}\nfootnotes: [] (none)\n\nTable 4 (DM):\nrows: {\"type\": \"DM (S)\", 0.3, \"4\\\" (DN 100)\", 5.75, 200, 2500, 200}\nMaybe merge Tables 3 and 4 into one matrix_table? They're separate tables (BMxx and DM). I'll keep two tables; or combine with same columns — combining is fine too. I'll keep separate to mirror the document. Actually combining into one \"Meter characteristics (types DM and BMxx)\" reduces duplication. I'll keep separate for fidelity.\n\nTable 6 (sensors) — complex. Flatten to rows per (type, variant, class):\n\ncolumns: [\"type\", \"variant\", \"accuracy_class\", \"qmin\", \"qmax\", \"mmq\", \"maximum_pressure\"]\ncolumn_units: [null, null, null, \"kg/min\", \"kg/min\", \"kg\", \"bar(g)\"]\n\nrows:\nCMF010: variant null (material via y code), class 0.3: qmin \"0.033 (1); 0.067 (2)\", qmax 1.8, mmq 0.05, p \"125 (3); 225 (4); 413 (2)\"\nclass 0.5: qmin \"0.017 (1); 0.033 (2)\", same qmax/mmq/p\nRather than repeat qmax per class, produce rows per class with repeated values (fine).\n\nLet me write rows:\n1. {\"type\": \"CMF010\", \"accuracy_class\": 0.3, \"qmin\": \"0.033 (1); 0.067 (2)\", \"qmax\": 1.8, \"mmq\": 0.05, \"maximum